{"assets":["/statement-assets/e2a45ea8a893e09f50f00adbb6a174d79b3a911f2158d1c4d774f3d44e139b25.png","/statement-assets/af4bc51fb559cc827303c081cfdaf8e44f3a497fb091648580c437ff35369f37.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"750","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. New Year and Finding Roots"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This is an interactive problem. In the interaction section below you will find the information about flushing the output."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The New Year tree of height "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a perfect binary tree with vertices numbered "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" through "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2h - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" in some order. In this problem we assume that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h"},{"kind":"text","text":" is at least "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":". The drawing below shows one example New Year tree of height "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/e2a45ea8a893e09f50f00adbb6a174d79b3a911f2158d1c4d774f3d44e139b25.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Polar bears love decorating the New Year tree and Limak is no exception. To decorate the tree, he must first find its root, i.e. a vertex with exactly two neighbours (assuming that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h ≥ 2"},{"kind":"text","text":"). It won't be easy because Limak is a little bear and he doesn't even see the whole tree. Can you help him?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" testcases. In each testcase, you should first read "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h"},{"kind":"text","text":" from the input. Then you can ask at most "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"16"},{"kind":"text","text":" questions of format \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"? x"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without quotes), where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" is an integer between "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2h - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", inclusive. As a reply you will get the list of neighbours of vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" (more details in the \"Interaction\" section below). For example, for a tree on the drawing above after asking \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"? 1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" you would get a response with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":" neighbours: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"7"},{"kind":"text","text":". Your goal is to find the index of the root "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":" and print it in the format \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"! y"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". You will be able to read "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h"},{"kind":"text","text":" for a next testcase only after printing the answer in a previous testcase and flushing the output."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each tree is fixed from the beginning and it doesn't change during your questions."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ t ≤ 500"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of testcases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"At the beginning of each testcase you should read from the input a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ h ≤ 7"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the height of the tree. You can't read the value of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h"},{"kind":"text","text":" in a next testcase until you answer a previous testcase."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"custom","title":"Interaction"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Interaction"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To ask a question about neighbours of vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":", print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"? x"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without quotes) on a separate line. Note, you must print an end-of-line character after the last character of the line and flush your output to get a response."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The response will consist of two lines. The first line will contain a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ k ≤ 3"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of neighbours of vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":". The second line will contain "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" distinct integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t1, ..., tk"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ t1 < ... < tk ≤ 2h - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":") — indices of neighbours of vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":", gives in the increasing order."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After asking at most "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"16"},{"kind":"text","text":" questions you have to say "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the index of the root. Print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"! y"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without quotes) and an end-of-line character, and flush the output."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each tree is fixed from the beginning and it doesn't change during your questions."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can get "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Idleness Limit Exceeded"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if you don't print anything or if you forget to flush the output."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To flush you can use (just printing a query/answer and end-of-line): "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fflush(stdout)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in C++; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"System.out.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Java; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"stdout.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Python; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"flush(output)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Pascal; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" See the documentation for other languages. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In any moment if the program reads "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h = 0"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k = 0"},{"kind":"text","text":" it should immediately terminate normally (for example, calling exit(0)). It means that the system detected incorrect request/output from your program and printed 0 because if can't process your requests anymore. In this case you'll receive verdict \"Wrong Answer\", but if you ignore case "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h = 0"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k = 0"},{"kind":"text","text":" it could lead to \"Runtime Error\", \"Time/Memory limit exceeded\" or any other verdict because your program could read a trash from the closed input stream."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Hacking"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". To hack someone, use the following format:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line should contain a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" (only one testcase is allowed in hacks). The second line should contain a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h"},{"kind":"text","text":". Each of next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2h - 2"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines should contain two distinct integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bi"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ai, bi ≤ 2h - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":"), denoting two nodes connected with an edge. The printed edges must form a perfect binary tree of height "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Of course, contestant programs will not be able to see this input."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n3\n3\n4 5 7\n2\n1 2\n1\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"? 1\n? 5\n? 6\n! 5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n2\n1\n3\n2\n1 2\n2\n1 2\n4\n3\n3 12 13\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"? 1\n? 3\n? 3\n! 3\n? 6\n! 1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample, a tree corresponds to the drawing from the statement."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample, there are two two testcases. A tree in the first testcase has height "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" and thus "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertices. A tree in the second testcase has height "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":" and thus "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"15"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertices. You can see both trees on the drawing below."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/af4bc51fb559cc827303c081cfdaf8e44f3a497fb091648580c437ff35369f37.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"750F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/750/problem/F"}